From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:45:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Signals: FEX's host handlers block every other signal while
 they run

A host handler's mask was the guest's sa_mask for that signal, so a guest
signal could land inside FEX's own handler code, e.g. a SIGUSR1 during the
host SIGILL that carries a guest rt_sigreturn (which Linux can't
interrupt): it was taken for interrupted C++ code and its ContextBackup
written below the interrupted SP, over the host signal stack in use,
corrupting the saved registers. A thread taking trapped SIGSYS (syscall
user dispatch, SECCOMP_RET_TRAP) while being sent SIGUSR1 died by SIGSEGV
within seconds. Now every non-required signal is blocked during the host
handler; the guest handler still gets the guest's mask through the
uc_sigmask FEX writes into the frame.
---
 .../Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
index be73f92..e1f1d68 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
@@ -917,11 +917,14 @@ bool SignalDelegator::UpdateHostThunk(int Signal) {
   // Walk the signals we have that are required and make sure to remove it from the mask
   // This'll likely be SIGILL, SIGBUS, SIG63
 
-  // If the guest has masked some signals then we need to also mask those signals
+  // Every other signal stays blocked while FEX's own handler code runs, not only the guest's sa_mask: that code is not
+  // reentrant. A guest signal landing in it (a SIGUSR1 during the host SIGILL that carries a guest rt_sigreturn, which
+  // Linux can't interrupt) was taken for interrupted C++ code and its frame written over the host signal stack in use.
+  // The guest handler still runs with the guest's mask: that one is the uc_sigmask FEX writes into the frame.
   for (size_t i = 1; i < HostHandlers.size(); ++i) {
     if (HostHandlers[i].Required.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
       SignalHandler.HostAction.sa_mask &= ~(1ULL << (i - 1));
-    } else if (SigIsMember(&SignalHandler.GuestAction.sa_mask, i)) {
+    } else {
       SignalHandler.HostAction.sa_mask |= (1ULL << (i - 1));
     }
   }
